" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278584 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1089 "q-320730" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1100 "Expressed in degrees, $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=${{field-1}}${}^{∘}.$" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1113 #uuid "f53bc9c3-fd24-580b-be8a-fd85b0a8922e" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278583 1145 "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}<\\theta <{90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the fourth quadrant, where the tangent is negative.\n\nFrom the special values of the trigonometric functions and the oddness of the tangent function, we know that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-{30}^{∘})=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{∘}$ is an angle in the fourth quadrant that lies within the range of $arctan,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})={-30}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278585 13194139534144 true] [17592186278584 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534144 true] [17592186278584 1041 "field-1" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278584 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278585 13194139534144 true] [17592186278584 1110 #uuid "b6baa3ed-3895-59e1-a671-f7ca80a57681" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278585 1034 "-30" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534144 true] [17592186278585 1111 #uuid "8fea6824-130d-568a-8b22-651d4b7f4508" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278587 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1089 "q-82179" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1100 "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=$" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1113 #uuid "3b74ba82-3450-586d-bec9-151c983d04a4" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278586 1145 "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{∘}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978511/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡({300}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, ${300}^{∘}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with ${300}^{∘}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract ${360}^{∘}.$\n\n$$\n{300}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=-{60}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278588 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278589 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278590 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278591 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278592 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1041 "selection" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278591 13194139534144 true] [17592186278587 1110 #uuid "caf0c747-d226-5dd8-89fb-ae2aa8599de0" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278588 1034 "-{90}^{∘}" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534144 true] [17592186278588 1111 #uuid "521e0961-320b-53aa-8dcf-420ec8d76bed" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278589 1034 "-{30}^{∘}" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534144 true] [17592186278589 1111 #uuid "824397f3-bb67-56d1-9fe3-65a62945f249" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278590 1034 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139534144 true] [17592186278590 1103 #edb/